# Ignored paths a build, an install or an IDE puts back. `talea prune` reads
# this as one more attributes file — git's own matcher, git's own syntax — so a
# merged worktree holding only these is not kept for "ignored files you made".
#
# Adding an ecosystem is adding lines here; no code changes. A repo can say
# `-talea-regenerable` in its own .gitattributes to take one back, and a
# developer can add patterns for every repo in git's global attributes file
# (`git config --global core.attributesFile`).
#
# A folder is `**/<name>/**`: without the leading `**/` the pattern is anchored
# to the repo root and misses `ios/Flutter/ephemeral/`. A pattern with a slash
# in it is anchored; one without matches a basename at any depth. A leading `/`
# matches nothing in an attributes file — write `a/b`, not `/a/b`.

# JavaScript and the web
**/node_modules/** talea-regenerable
**/dist/** talea-regenerable
**/.next/** talea-regenerable
**/.nuxt/** talea-regenerable
**/.turbo/** talea-regenerable
**/.astro/** talea-regenerable
**/.cache/** talea-regenerable
**/coverage/** talea-regenerable
**/.firebase/** talea-regenerable

# Python
**/.venv/** talea-regenerable
**/venv/** talea-regenerable
**/__pycache__/** talea-regenerable
**/.pytest_cache/** talea-regenerable

# Rust, Gradle, CocoaPods, and every build folder
**/target/** talea-regenerable
**/.gradle/** talea-regenerable
**/.kotlin/** talea-regenerable
**/Pods/** talea-regenerable
**/build/** talea-regenerable

# Flutter and Dart: what `flutter pub get` and `flutter build` write, with
# absolute paths and plugin versions in it, so it never matches the main
# checkout's copy byte for byte.
**/.dart_tool/** talea-regenerable
**/ephemeral/** talea-regenerable
**/.symlinks/** talea-regenerable
**/.plugin_symlinks/** talea-regenerable
.flutter-plugins talea-regenerable
.flutter-plugins-dependencies talea-regenerable
local.properties talea-regenerable
Generated.xcconfig talea-regenerable
flutter_export_environment.sh talea-regenerable
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.* talea-regenerable
pubspec.lock talea-regenerable
Podfile.lock talea-regenerable

# IDEs and the OS
**/.idea/** talea-regenerable
*.iml talea-regenerable
.DS_Store talea-regenerable

# Seeded by worktree tooling as a copy of the main checkout's.
.claude/settings.local.json talea-regenerable
